# KALUA Agentic Development — Cursor Rules

The canonical authoring guide is `docs/agentic/development.md`.

## Commands

- `./KALUA check app.lua` — static validation (syntax, unknown k.*, main)
- `./KALUA run app.lua --test --json` — headless run-mode test
- `./KALUA serve app.lua --test --json` — headless serve-mode smoke
- `./KALUA new app --template serve-all` — scaffold (run-form, run-crud, serve-http, serve-ws, serve-tcp, serve-all)
- `./KALUA ai generate "..." -o app.lua --mode run|serve` — AI generate
- `./KALUA ai fix app.lua --mode run|serve` — AI fix
- `./KALUA lsp` — LSP over stdio
- `./KALUA mcp` — MCP server (stdio, protocol 2025-06-18)
- `./KALUA builder app.lua` — visual form builder

## Rules

1. **Always validate**: `check` → `run/serve --test` before assuming correctness
2. **Prefer KALUA APIs**: `k.*` / `K.*` / expression functions (`left`, `upper`, `round`, `sys_date`, `k.http_request`, ...) over generic Lua
3. **Run-mode shape**: `function main()` + `k.form.new` + `k.form.show` + `k.form.on` handlers
4. **Serve-mode shape**: `handle_http(req)` / `handle_ws(msg)` / `handle_tcp(msg)` + optional `init`/`shutdown` — **no UI bindings**
5. **Exit codes**: 0=OK, 1=Error, 2=Usage, 3=IO
6. **Machine-readable**: `--json` on `check`, `run --test`, `serve --test`, `new`

